# ASTRA's review controls write their observations into evidence/. Several do
# it with a bare write_text and no mkdir at all, so the DIRECTORY has to exist
# in the tree or the control dies with FileNotFoundError before it reaches an
# assertion -- which is how #164's CI produced 67 red rows carrying no product
# signal. The rule was `evidence/`, which ignores the directory itself, and git
# does not descend into an ignored directory, so nothing inside it could be
# kept. It is the CONTENTS that are run output, not the directory.
/evidence/*
!/evidence/.gitkeep
